  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper reports shallow quantum-kernel QSVC and QSVR experiments on IonQ trapped-ion hardware and simulators. QSVC used 4 qubits with 500 shots per kernel entry and achieved 70%, 100%, and 100% test accuracy on credit-card fraud, MNIST, and Fashion-MNIST, matching classical SVM on test performance; QSVR on IonQ Harmony reached R2=0.868 (financial) and 0.628 (materials), below classical SVR at 0.930 and 0.728. Supplementary results also include noisy-simulation robustness studies and an IonQ Aria run with 8 qubits achieving 100% Fashion-MNIST test accuracy.",
